@startuml connection
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam shadowing false
title Connection Authorization and Recovery

state "Disconnected\nconnected = false" as Disconnected
state "Connecting\ncaptures a new connectionID" as Connecting
state "Waiting for folder authorization\nenable() returns false" as Picker
state "Connected\nenabled = true / connected = true" as Connected
state "Unavailable\nconnected = false / error shown\nenabled keeps the user's intent" as Failed
state "Disabled\nenabled = false / connected = false" as Disabled

[*] --> Disconnected
Disconnected --> Connecting : enable / connect (picked folder)
Disabled --> Connecting : enable again
Connecting --> Picker : no saved bookmark and no iCloud container
Picker --> Connecting : user picks a folder → connect(to:)
Picker --> Disconnected : authorization not completed
Connecting --> Connected : device identity, folder and repository valid\nactivate → periodic task → folder observation → immediate sync
Connecting --> Failed : restore / authorization / validation failed
Connected --> Connected : ordinary domain error\nrecord error and retry work
Connected --> Failed : sync hits SyncError.unavailable\ninvalidateConnection → repository.disconnect
Failed --> Connecting : reconnect / re-authorize
Connected --> Connecting : replace folder / reconnect
Connected --> Disabled : disable()
Failed --> Disabled : disable()
Connecting --> Disabled : superseded by turning sync off
Connected --> Disabled : iCloud identity changed\nalso clears login sharing consent, bookmark and identity token

note right of Connecting
  invalidateConnection runs before every new connection:
  1. new connectionID; clear remote lists and pending work
  2. cancel coalescing / execution / periodic tasks
  3. invalidate continue requests and publication baselines
  4. disconnect the previous repository connection

  enable: bookmark → restore; otherwise try the container.
  connect: the picked root or its Kite subfolder.
  restore never re-creates a deleted authorized folder.
end note
note right of Connected
  The picked-folder and restore entry points each start
  one security scope, owned by repository.scopedURL on success.
  The iCloud container needs no security scope.
  Released on disconnect or when the entry point fails.

  After every await the operation's connection is checked;
  a stale operation can neither activate nor clear its replacement.
end note
note bottom of Disabled
  A plain disable does not withdraw cloud files or sign out remotely.
  The local account, playback restore and saved preferences remain.
end note
@enduml
